Preserve a push-button gadget's resolved fontList.

XmPushButtonGadget's InitializePrehook overwrote an already-resolved font
(from XmNfontList / XmNrenderTable resources) with the inherited button
default render table, because the guard was inverted. XmeGetDefaultRenderTable
walks to the parent for XmBUTTON_FONTLIST, so a push button in a menu lost its
own fontList and fell back to the ancestor default, which resolves to the
monospace "fixed" font. Toggle and cascade gadgets have no such prehook, so a
single pulldown rendered its push items monospace while toggles and cascades
stayed proportional. Match the base class (LabelG.c) and the sibling path at
PushBG.c:2087, which correctly set the default only when no font is present.

diff --git a/lib/Xm/PushBG.c b/lib/Xm/PushBG.c
index 26dad283..f76287a4 100644
--- a/lib/Xm/PushBG.c
+++ b/lib/Xm/PushBG.c
@@ -1771,6 +1771,6 @@ SecondaryObjectCreate(
 static void InitializePrehook(Widget req, Widget new_w, ArgList args,
                               Cardinal *num_args)
 {
-	if (LabG_Font(new_w))
+	if (!LabG_Font(new_w))
 		LabG_Font(new_w) = XmeGetDefaultRenderTable(new_w, XmBUTTON_FONTLIST);
 }
